 },
 "lines": {
  "hook": "Your car just died in the desert. You have one bottle of water.",
  "b1": "Do you save it, or drink it?",
  "b2": "In this heat, you can sweat out a liter every hour.",
  "b3": "Instinct says save it. But ration it, and the heat can take you down with water still in the bottle.",
  "b4": "So sip it, early and often. Water works in your body, not in the bottle.",
  "b5": "Don't ration your water. Ration your sweat.",
  "b6": "One. Cover up. Clothes block the sun and make your sweat last.",
  "b7": "Two. Find shade, and get off the ground. The sand is far hotter than the air.",
  "b8": "Three. Stay with the car. It's much easier to spot than you.",
  "end": "So, save it or drink it? Tell me which one you picked."
 },
